A Programmer needs to implement a third-person camera that can rotate around the player character by moving the mouse. The following code is attached to the camera:

```csharp
public class CameraController : MonoBehaviour
{
    public Transform TargetPlayer { get; set; }
    public float CamOffset { get; set; }

    private Vector3 _rotationResult;
    private Vector3 _currentRotation;
    private float _yaw;
    private float _pitch;

    private void LateUpdate()
    {
        _yaw += Input.GetAxis("Mouse X");
        _pitch -= Input.GetAxis("Mouse Y");
        _currentRotation = Vector3.SmoothDamp(_currentRotation, new Vector3(_pitch, _yaw), ref _rotationResult, 0.5f);
        transform.eulerAngles = _currentRotation;
        transform.position = TargetPlayer.position - transform.forward * CamOffset;
    }
}
```
The camera works as intended, except that the camera has no limit on its pitch rotation and can potentially rotate nonstop if the user keeps moving the mouse.

What should the Programmer do to prevent this behavior?

